WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.357
A complete sales CRM that turns every website signup into a lead, and helps your team follow up and close the deal.

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:13.499
After signing in, the home screen shows what matters today.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:21.416
New leads, leads still waiting for a first call, the open pipeline, recent wins, and the tasks that are due.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:26.245
Here is a company website with an ordinary signup form.

00:00:26.396 --> 00:00:29.296
One line of code connects it to the CRM.

00:00:29.615 --> 00:00:37.477
When a visitor signs up, the website keeps working exactly as before, and a copy of their details goes straight into the CRM.

00:00:42.902 --> 00:00:45.796
The snippet comes from Settings, Website forms.

00:00:45.946 --> 00:00:53.381
You can also post a plain HTML form, call the API from your own server, or share a hosted form link.

00:00:53.532 --> 00:00:57.397
It works with WordPress, Webflow, Wix, and custom websites.

00:00:59.441 --> 00:01:02.273
The new lead is already here, at the top of the list.

00:01:02.424 --> 00:01:06.007
Every lead gets an automatic score, from cold to hot.

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:11.977
You can search, filter by status, rating, source or owner, and update many leads at once.

00:01:17.347 --> 00:01:19.960
Open a lead to see everything about them.

00:01:20.111 --> 00:01:27.858
Contact details, custom fields like the number of stores, marketing consent, and where they came from, including the campaign.

00:01:29.068 --> 00:01:33.890
Log calls, meetings, notes and WhatsApp conversations on the timeline.

00:01:36.443 --> 00:01:39.155
Then add a follow-up task, so nothing slips.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:47.054
Send an email straight from the lead, using a template.

00:01:47.444 --> 00:01:52.657
The details fill in automatically, and you can see when the email is opened and clicked.

00:01:53.568 --> 00:01:55.511
Sequences follow up for you.

00:02:02.903 --> 00:02:09.310
A welcome email today, a reminder after two days, a call task on day five, and a final check-in.

00:02:09.645 --> 00:02:15.562
They stop on their own when the person replies by phone, unsubscribes, or becomes a customer.

00:02:16.768 --> 00:02:19.879
When a lead is qualified, convert it with one click.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:27.612
The CRM creates the contact, the company and a deal, and carries the whole history across.

00:02:29.973 --> 00:02:35.818
The pipeline shows every open deal by stage, with the total and weighted value of each column.

00:02:35.969 --> 00:02:37.771
Drag a deal to move it forward.

00:02:38.505 --> 00:02:42.024
Deals that have gone quiet are flagged, so they get attention.

00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:49.447
Inside a deal, click a stage to move it, or mark it won or lost with a reason.

00:02:49.871 --> 00:02:53.435
Quotes, tasks and every conversation are in one place.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:58.994
Build a quote from your product list, with tax and discount worked out for you.

00:03:04.385 --> 00:03:07.538
Then share a customer link, or email it directly.

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:15.975
Your customer opens a clean page, reviews the quote, types their name, and accepts it online.

00:03:18.942 --> 00:03:22.564
You are notified when they open it, and the moment they accept.

00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:25.167
The deal is marked as won automatically.

00:03:26.401 --> 00:03:29.034
Every salesperson can have a booking page.

00:03:29.185 --> 00:03:34.451
Choose your days, hours and meeting length, then share the link or embed it on your website.

00:03:35.368 --> 00:03:38.259
Prospects pick a day and a time that suits them.

00:03:38.592 --> 00:03:44.888
The booking creates the lead, adds a meeting to your tasks, and sends a confirmation with a calendar invite.

00:03:48.303 --> 00:03:50.371
Tasks keep the whole team on track.

00:03:50.524 --> 00:03:56.948
See what is overdue, due today, and coming up. Reminders arrive in the app, by email, and on Telegram.

00:03:59.525 --> 00:04:06.839
Contacts and companies keep each customer relationship together, with every deal and conversation on one timeline.

00:04:09.068 --> 00:04:14.053
Reports show your revenue forecast by month, the lead funnel, and a team leaderboard.

00:04:14.205 --> 00:04:19.561
You can also see why deals are lost, and which sources and campaigns bring in customers.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:23.066
Automations save hours every week.

00:04:23.828 --> 00:04:31.989
For example, when a new lead arrives with a big budget, add them to a sequence. You choose the trigger, the conditions, and the actions.

00:04:34.368 --> 00:04:37.687
Make the CRM fit your business with custom fields.

00:04:37.838 --> 00:04:43.139
Add dropdowns, numbers, dates and amounts to leads, contacts, companies and deals.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.564
Invite your team with a link, and give each person a role.

00:04:53.564 --> 00:04:58.607
Turn on two-step sign-in with any authenticator app, and require it for everyone.

00:05:03.568 --> 00:05:07.394
Privacy tools help you follow India's data protection law.

00:05:07.546 --> 00:05:16.054
Consent is recorded, every marketing email has an unsubscribe link, and you can export or erase a person's data in one click.

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:22.517
Add your logo and brand colour. They appear in the app, on quotes, booking pages and forms.

00:05:22.669 --> 00:05:24.473
And there is a dark mode too.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.866
The CRM works on phones, and can be installed like an app.

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:45.953
Developers get a full API with documentation, personal tokens, and webhooks for Slack, Discord, Google Sheets and more.

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:51.150
Capture every lead, follow up automatically, and close more deals.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:52.873
Thank you for watching.
